## Session 31 Summary

**Criterion (`./run.sh 2 tcp` 100%) NOT met** — `dir_reuse_coherency` still fails (16/17). Marker **not** written (honest).

### Real progress this session

**FIXED one of the failure faces (FACE B) — verified, regression-free.** The inode-revert / `P26-IGET-FAIL` / `lookup_fail` face: a dirent pointed at an inode that read **free** in-core while the coherent disk showed it **live** (`cached_disk_mode=0x81a4`). Root: the `P116-RELOAD-SELFCLOBBER-SKIP` guard kept the in-core inode only when **dirty**, but by verify-time the node's own create is checkpointed-clean, so the reload adopted the stale-free disk image and reverted the node's own live inode → ENOENT.

**Fix (build `5E706CBF`, KEEP):** in `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode`, keep the in-core inode when the node **still holds the DLM grant** (`i_dlm_mode != MXFS_LOCK_NL`) — grant ownership, not dirtiness, is the authority (per the `i_dlm_epoch` invariant; node-affine inode alloc makes a held grant authoritative). Result: `P-RELOAD-IOPS-REWIRE new_mode=00 = 0×`, `P26-IGET-FAIL = 0×`, and cache_coherency / zero_silent_loss / crash_consistency all **PASS 2/2** (no regression).

### Remaining blocker fully diagnosed
Sole residual = **dir-DATA-block first-wave dirent loss** (`readdir ~185/200`, e.g. node1_f1..f12). Confirmed **all** release/acquire architectural fixes are already present and working (CIL-force + drain + stale on release; force-evict default on acquire). Refuted `dirskip=1` (hangs).

### Two GPT-5.5 consults (RULE 5)
1st confirmed the release-side CIL-force architecture (already implemented). 2nd identified the likely root: either (a) `xfs_trans_read_buf` returns a **cached stale XBF_DONE** block 0, or (b) a **stale inode data-fork** makes the node treat block 0 as new → `xfs_dir3_data_init` (get_buf) **zeroes a reused daddr holding the peer's durable dirents** (ABA). The "bounded-wait-then-skip pinned dir buffer" is the core correctness hole.

### Left ready for next session
Build **`63035077`** = FACE B fix + log-only **P31E-DATAINIT-ABA detector** (`xfs_dir3_data_init`). Next: run `dir_reuse_coherency`, grep `P31E-DATAINIT-ABA`. If it **fires** → stale-inode-fork ABA confirmed (fix = refresh dir inode fork at acquire); if **not** → cached-stale-read path (fix = force cold-read of block 0, never skip a pinned old-epoch base). Exact instructions + GPT verdicts in memory `sess31-GPT2-ABA-datainit-detector-next-run`. Three KEEP detectors and the FACE B fix carry forward.

